\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366214 1113 #uuid "c3f26762-2007-5a70-9751-caae5ca04520" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366214 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+{e}^{1/2} \\\\  & ≈3.648\\,721,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y≈3.648\\,721.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & ≈2\\cdot 3.648\\,721+{e}^{1} \\\\  & ≈10.015\\,724,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, rounded to $2$ decimal places, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈3.65,\\,y(1)≈10.02.\n$$" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366216 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366217 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366218 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1041 "field-1" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366216 13194139535785 true] [17592186366215 1110 #uuid "1a6d13c7-7e47-5f91-8965-3d05c4467012" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366216 1034 "3.65" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535785 true] [17592186366216 1111 #uuid "46a37d9d-19bc-5c83-baba-1f1c47491d05" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366217 1034 "2.00" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535785 true] [17592186366217 1111 #uuid "9e6f58f8-b191-5ac3-83fd-a7c8ed6282c7" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366218 1034 "1.73" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535785 true] [17592186366218 1111 #uuid "28ac9ec4-ef2b-5977-90a1-cb28718b0079" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366220 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366221 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366222 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1041 "field-2" 13194139535785 true] [17592186366219 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366